#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:1
msgid "ROS 2 Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:3
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to Integrate ROS 2 with Ignition. We will "
"establish communication between them. This can help in many aspects; we can "
"receive data or commands from ROS and apply it to Ignition and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:7
msgid "ros_ign_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:9
msgid ""
"`ros_ign_bridge` provides a network bridge which enables the exchange of "
"messages between ROS 2 and Ignition Transport. Its support is limited to "
"only certain message types. Please, check this [README](https://github.com/"
"ignitionrobotics/ros_ign/blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md) to verify if "
"your message type is supported by the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:11
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:13
msgid ""
"For this tutorial to work correctly make sure you have the following "
"installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:15
msgid "[ROS 2 Foxy](https://index.ros.org/doc/ros2/Installation/Foxy/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:16
msgid "[Ignition Dome](https://gazebosim.org/docs/dome)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:17
msgid ""
"[ros_ign_bridge](https://github.com/ignitionrobotics/ros_ign/tree/ros2#from-"
"source)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:19
msgid "Bidirectional communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:21
msgid ""
"We can initialize a bidirectional bridge so we can have ROS as the publisher "
"and Ignition as the subscriber or vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:23
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:25
msgid "ros2 run ros_ign_bridge parameter_bridge /TOPIC@ROS_MSG@IGN_MSG\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:29
msgid ""
"The `ros2 run ros_ign_bridge parameter_bridge` command simply runs the "
"`parameter_bridge` code from the `ros_ign_bridge` package. Then, we specify "
"our topic `/TOPIC` over which the messages will be sent. The first `@` "
"symbol delimits the topic name from the message types. Following the first "
"`@` symbol is the ROS message type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:31
msgid "The ROS message type is followed by an `@`, `[`, or `]` symbol where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:33
msgid "`@`  is a bidirectional bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:34
msgid "`[`  is a bridge from Ignition to ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:35
msgid "`]`  is a bridge from ROS to Ignition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:37
msgid ""
"Have a look at these [examples](https://github.com/ignitionrobotics/ros_ign/"
"blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md#example-1a-ignition-transport-talker-and-"
"ros-2-listener) explaining how to make communication connections from ROS to "
"Ignition and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:40
msgid "Publish key strokes to ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:42
msgid ""
"Let's send messages to ROS using the `Key Publisher` an Ignition plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:44
msgid ""
"**Note:** Make sure to have all workspaces you need (ROS, Ignition and, "
"`ros_ign`...) sourced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:47
msgid ""
"First we will start a bridge between ROS and Ignition specifying the topic "
"at which the `Key Publisher` plugin sends messages and also the type of the "
"messages as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:51
msgid ""
"ros2 run ros_ign_bridge parameter_bridge /keyboard/keypress@std_msgs/msg/"
"Int32@ignition.msgs.Int32\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:55
msgid ""
"We started a bridge on `/keyboard/keypress` topic with message of type "
"`Int32`. For ROS it is `std_msgs/msg/Int32` and for Ignition it is `ignition."
"msgs.Int32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:58
msgid ""
"In another terminal launch an Gazebo Sim world, for example the `empty.sdf` "
"world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:60
msgid "ign gazebo empty.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:64
msgid ""
"Then add the `Key Publisher` plugin from the dropdown menu on the top right "
"corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:66
msgid ""
"![empty_world_with_KeyPublisher](tutorials/ros2_integration/empty_world.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:66
msgid "empty_world_with_KeyPublisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:68
msgid "In another terminal start the ROS listener:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:70
msgid "ros2 topic echo /keyboard/keypress\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:74
msgid ""
"This command listens to the messages sent over the `/keyboard/keypress` "
"topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:76
msgid ""
"On the Ignition window, press on the keyboard keys and you should find data "
"on the listener terminal. This is what the terminals should look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:79
msgid "![exchange_messages](tutorials/ros2_integration/ros_ign.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:79
msgid "exchange_messages"
msgstr ""

